# PyGObject -- the Python binding for GObject introspection, and it is here for
# exactly one reason: libgweather cannot be built without it.
#
# NOT A CHOICE ABOUT PYTHON SUPPORT ON THE DESKTOP. libgweather's
# data/meson.build runs build-aux/meson/gen_locations_variant.py as an
# UNCONDITIONAL custom_target -- install:true, no option, no guard -- to
# generate the Locations.bin it ships, and that script's fifth line is
# `from gi.repository import GLib`. So a weather library needs a Python binding
# at build time, which is not a sentence anybody would predict from either
# dependency page. BLFS lists PyGObject as Required for libgweather for the same
# reason.
#
# Measured before packaging rather than assumed: in a container seeded with the
# published set, `python3 -c "from gi.repository import GLib"` is
# ModuleNotFoundError and there is no `gi` anywhere under /usr/lib/python3* --
# Duct's python is built --without-ensurepip, so it has no third-party modules
# at all unless one is packaged.
#
# BLFS 12.4 (PyGObject-3.52.3), pinned here rather than in versions.env: that
# file is regenerated wholesale from the LFS book by tools/pin-versions.sh.
# The sha256 below is upstream's OWN published digest -- pygobject-3.52.3.sha256sum
# from the same directory -- rather than a book md5, which is the stronger check
# of the two.
SRC_URL=https://download.gnome.org/sources/pygobject/3.52/pygobject-3.52.3.tar.gz
SRC_SHA256=00e427d291e957462a8fad659a9f9c8be776ff82a8b76bdf402f1eaeec086d82
SRC_DIR=pygobject-3.52.3

# -Dtests=false. The option defaults TRUE, and with it on meson.build:223 calls
# `subproject('gobject-introspection-tests')`. This tarball DOES ship that
# directory for real (34 entries, checked -- it is not a download-only wrap), so
# it would resolve under --wrap-mode=nodownload rather than failing. It is
# turned off anyway because it is build time spent on a test suite nothing runs,
# and because the same block then requires gobject-introspection-1.0, which this
# package otherwise does not need at all.
#
# -Dpycairo=disabled. The option is a `feature` defaulting AUTO, and pycairo is
# not packaged -- so auto resolves to off today and would switch itself on the
# day anybody packages it, changing this artefact with no change to this recipe.
# Nothing here wants it: the one consumer draws no cairo surfaces from Python,
# it serialises a GVariant.
#
# WHAT THIS PACKAGE NEEDS AND WHERE IT COMES FROM, because the obvious answer is
# wrong: meson.build:31 is `dependency('girepository-2.0', ...)`, NOT
# girepository-1.0 -- glib 2.80 absorbed girepository, and in this tree
# girepository-2.0.pc and libgirepository-2.0.so are shipped by the GLIB
# package, not by gobject-introspection. Checked by listing both published
# artefacts rather than by reasoning about which project owns the name. So the
# core build needs glib, libffi and python, and gobject-introspection is a
# test-only edge that -Dtests=false removes.
MESON_ARGS="-Dtests=false -Dpycairo=disabled -Dwheel=false"
